      "steps": [
        "Inspect the supplied aging record, apply the requested policy and check every dated observation while preserving history and protected accounts."
      ],
      "guide": [],
      "explanation": "The maximum and warning are independent metadata fields. With the supplied last-change history,45 days reaches the assignment deadline and 10 days gives advance notice. -M and -W change those fields without faking a recent password change. The state and all dated cases, including the end of the existing grace, are checked; all-disabled policy is not an equivalent solution.",
      "hints": [
        "First list morgan with chage -l morgan. Maximum age and warning are two separate fields.",
        "Use capital -M for maximum days and -W for warning days; changing -d would alter the supplied history.",
        "Compare the warning-start date with the maximum-age date. The warning adds notice, not more valid days."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://www.lpi.org/our-certifications/exam-101-102-objectives/",
        "https://github.com/shadow-maint/shadow/blob/4.18.0/man/chage.1.xml",
        "https://github.com/linux-pam/linux-pam/blob/v1.7.1/modules/pam_unix/passverify.c"
      ],
      "simplifications": "Checked 2026-11-08: LPIC-1 v5.0 / 107.1 and 110.1; shadow 4.18.0 metadata options and Linux-PAM v1.7.1 expiry-helper ordering. Supplied non-secret virtual records and explicit UTC dates only. chage lists metadata; the separate observation table models one versioned aging policy, not universal login access. The pinned helper uses >= at exact expiry dates; manual wording differs. No passwords/hashes, actual password change, PAM/NSS/LDAP, host accounts/files/clock/processes or real authentication. ISO-only query output; bounded disclosed options, no interactive/root/prefix/short clusters/shell syntax. Ordinary day 0 / 1970-01-01 is excluded; lastday 0 is the explicit reset marker. Other account utilities stay in their existing workspaces.",
      "prerequisites": [
        "lpic1-account-team-handover"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "AGING PLAN\n[\"chage -M 45 -W 10 morgan\"]"
      ]
    },
